## Requirements
- Node.js v18 or later
- MongoDB Atlas account
- npm

## 1) Clone and install
```bash
cd student-notes-manager
```

## 2) Backend setup
```bash
cd server
npm install
cp .env.example .env
```

Then open the `.env` file and replace the MongoDB connection string:

```env
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster.mongodb.net/student-notes-manager?retryWrites=true&w=majority
```

Start the backend:
```bash
npm run dev
```

The API should run at:
```bash
http://localhost:5000
```

## 3) Frontend setup
Open a new terminal and run:
```bash
cd student-notes-manager/client
npm install
npm run dev
```

The React app should run at:
```bash
http://localhost:5173
```

## 4) How to use the app
- Add a note with title, subject and content
- Search notes by title or subject
- Click Edit to change a note
- Click Delete to remove a note
- The app will show success or error messages

## API Endpoints
### Create note
```http
POST /api/notes
```

### Get all notes
```http
GET /api/notes
```

### Update note
```http
PUT /api/notes/:id
```

### Delete note
```http
DELETE /api/notes/:id
```

## Important note
Do not upload your real `.env` file to GitHub. Keep MongoDB credentials private.

## Beginner tip
- Frontend = what the user sees
- Backend = server that handles requests
- MongoDB = database where notes are stored
- Express = the server framework used to create API routes
- React = interface and form handling
- Axios = sends HTTP requests from frontend to backend

## Next Step
After you add your real MongoDB Atlas connection string, the app will save notes to the database and the CRUD operations will work.
